# Milestone: M3
# Covers: Barrier.new() synchronization primitive; multiple waiters unblocked
#         by signalAll/signal; interaction with tag stop.
# deferred: v1.x — Barrier stdlib type not in v1.0 scope
# matrix-row: stdlib-barrier
#
# Reason:
#   Barrier is a stdlib synchronization type scheduled for M6.  The fixture
#   also uses ',' (OP_FORK_DETACH) for parallel waiters, which requires the
#   urbi_step driver path (not available in the urbi_vm_run REPL).  Tag.new() method
#   dispatch (t.stop()) requires M4 object infrastructure.
#
# Original urbiscript (activate at M6 with full stdlib):
# # var b = Barrier.new() | {};
# # echo(b.wait()), echo(b.wait()), echo(b.wait()), sleep(0);
# # b.signalAll("foobar");
# # [00000001] 3
# # ... (see legacy/repos/aldebaran-urbi/tests/2.x/barrier.chk)
